classTweaker v1 official

# Flywheel 26.3 -- standalone module.
#
# Selection method (recorded so the set can be re-derived and audited):
#   1. take every create.classtweaker entry whose OWNER CLASS the Flywheel sources actually import;
#   2. drop Create's own content-registration API (Blocks.register/never, Fluids.register), which a
#      rendering library never touches;
#   3. add the supertype-dispatch cases a text scan cannot see (a member declared on a superclass but
#      invoked through a subclass receiver -- getPlayerInfo on AbstractClientPlayer via LocalPlayer);
#   4. whatever remains missing is appended as the compiler proves it missing.
#
# Over-inclusion here is harmless (an accessible entry only widens access); UNDER-inclusion is a hard
# compile error, so the set is verified by compiling the module, not by inspection.
#
# The GL entries are load-bearing: Flywheel's backend is GL-only and 26.3 exposes raw GL
# (GlDevice, the active texture unit, RenderType.create) only through the classtweaker.
